agent-learning README · DSH (main source)：Reviewers receive bounded packets in temporary directories and return structured candidates, with `ALP_DISABLED=1` to avoid plugin recursion. Codex skips user configuration and execpolicy rules, disables supported Hook, app, plugin, command and multi-agent capabilities, and uses a read-only sandbox. Read-only does not mean zero tools. Antigravity selects an empty-tool agent and sends evidence only after confirming `init.tools=[]` and `permission_mode=request-review`; it checks terminal ordering and discards thinking and intermediate text streams. DSH uses a fixed SDK module allowlist for one model request with no tools. It creates no Agent and loads no project Hooks, skills, rules or dynamic plugins. Its `--probe` checks SDK interfaces without initializing settings, authentication or a model.json
{
  "version": 1,
